The '''October 2026 Diet debate on the Wolffrean War''' was an emergency debate held in the [[House of Commoners of Okaiken]] on 23–24 October 2026. Convened amid escalating naval confrontation in the [[Pfein Sea]] and the regional spillover of the [[Wolffrean War]], the extraordinary plenary session was triggered by the 16 October artillery shelling of the Sanese-flagged commercial roll-on/roll-off carrier ''[[Aozora Maru]]'' off [[Mabanda]], the subsequent exposure of secret deconfliction communications on 20 October, and intelligence reports that [[Joint Working Group for Peace in Northern Kaftia]] (JWG-PNK) amphibious forces were assembling near the [[Strait of Sindewand]] for an imminent ground assault.

Faced with a fractured 253-seat coalition majority — a narrow 15-seat margin over the 238 required for governance — and confronting an imminent strike by the [[Okaiken Transport Workers' Union]] (OTWU), Prime Minister [[Kousuke Ikazaki]] ([[Sanese Communist Party|SCP]]) and Foreign Minister [[Kenichi Mori]] ([[Okaiken Socialist Party|OSP]]) introduced a comprehensive four-part '''"October Maritime Security and Non-Belligerence Legislative Package"'''. The package sought to reconcile the conflicting demands of constitutional pacifism, commercial mariner safety, and international humanitarian obligations under [[Adonian Community Resolution 4935]] and draft [[Adonian Community Resolution 4942D]].

== Background ==
{{Main|Wolffrean War|Wolffrean refugee crisis|Adonian Community Resolution 4940|Adonian Community Resolution 4942D}}

In September 2026, the [[Ikazaki Cabinet]] authorized the deployment of two destroyers of the [[Sanese Imperial Forces|SIF]] Escort Flotilla — including the ''ISN Shirakumo'' — and an auxiliary replenishment vessel to forward-stage in [[Alwana]]. Operating under the defensive provisions of the [[Kurosawa Doctrine]] and the humanitarian umbrella of [[Adonian Community Resolution 4935]], the Sanese naval group was tasked with escorting eleven Sanese-flagged commercial ferries chartered by the [[Adonian Community]] (AC) to evacuate civilians caught in the 17-million-person displacement catastrophe.

Okaiken's diplomatic position within the Adonian Assembly, however, became precarious following a series of divergent votes. On 24 September, Okaiken supported [[Adonian Community Resolution 4934]], endorsing indefinite pariah sanctions and the 1968 credential suspension against the State Mutualist government in [[Blumenaue]]. On 28 September, it cast a decisive abstention that defeated draft Resolution 4936, refusing to coerce [[Sindewand]] with sanctions over its historical border closures to [[White Wolffrean]] populations. On 11 October, it provided the deciding margin in the narrow 99–82 passage of [[Adonian Community Resolution 4938]], imposing targeted sanctions on [[Bonande]] following its unauthorized amphibious seizure of [[Mabanda]]. On 19 October, it abstained on [[Adonian Community Resolution 4940]], which authorized the JWG-PNK coalition to launch offensive air and naval strikes; Foreign Minister Mori defended the abstention before the international press with the words: "Okaiken will not vote for a war it does not intend to fight."

=== The 16 October attack and 20 October leak ===

On 16 October 2026, Bonandian shore artillery batteries stationed around Mabanda opened fire on maritime traffic, striking the chartered Sanese civilian ferry ''[[Aozora Maru]]''. The vessel suffered severe structural damage, and three Sanese merchant seamen were wounded by shrapnel.

To safeguard the evacuation fleet, Okaiken's consular mission in [[Yaweka]], headed by Consul [[Kurata Tomonori]], had quietly transmitted convoy coordinates simultaneously to coalition headquarters and through protecting intermediaries to Blumenaue. On 20 October, Staatsrat Chairman [[Merten Kruse-Essert]] leaked the coordination logs to the press, accusing Okami of "supplying coalition targeting grids under the guise of mercy." The leak destroyed the backchannel, leaving Sanese commercial hulls exposed to blind fire from both sides.

By 23 October, intelligence confirmed that JWG-PNK coalition forces were massing landing craft in the [[Strait of Sindewand]]. In Okami, the OTWU — representing over 1,200 Sanese seafarers deployed on the Pfein Sea sealift — threatened an immediate wildcat strike unless the cabinet either provided armed escort protection with clear rules of engagement or ordered an immediate withdrawal.

