== Plenary debates (23–24 October 2026) ==

The House of Commoners convened at 14:00 on 23 October under extraordinary tension. Crowds of anti-war demonstrators and OTWU trade union picketers gathered outside the Diet building in [[Chiyoda, Okami|Chiyoda]].

=== Interpellation of the Prime Minister ===

Leader of the Opposition [[Koichiro Sadanuma]] (LDP) opened the interpellations by attacking the Ikazaki Cabinet's handling of the 16 October attack:

<blockquote>
'''Koichiro Sadanuma (LDP):''' "Three Sanese sailors are lying in an Alwani field hospital with shrapnel torn through their bodies. The hull of the ''Aozora Maru'' is scorched by coastal artillery. And what is the response of the Prime Minister of Okaiken? A bureaucratic abstention! A quiet diplomatic whisper! Foreign Minister Mori tells the world that 'an abstention is a receipt.' But to our sailors, that receipt is signed in blood! When our civilian ships are bombarded in international waters, the Kurosawa Doctrine does not require us to cower behind the escarpments. Why has the government refused to authorize the ''ISN Shirakumo'' to return fire and eliminate those shore batteries? Is the life of a Sanese worker worth less than the ideological purity of the Communist Party?"
</blockquote>

Prime Minister [[Kousuke Ikazaki]] rose from the government frontbench to deliver a forceful defense of the administration's "Fortress State" (''Yōsai Kokka'') doctrine:

<blockquote>
'''Prime Minister Kousuke Ikazaki (SCP):''' "Mr. Sadanuma wants gunboat diplomacy. He wants us to order our destroyers to bombard the Kaftian mainland, drag this country into an unmandated war of partition, and turn our merchant mariners into target practice for every rogue coastal battery between Blumenaue and Mabanda. We refuse.<br /><br />
The attack on the ''Aozora Maru'' was an outrage, and this government has already issued an unsparing diplomatic dressing down to both the Bonandian and Wolffrean missions in Okami. But let this House be completely clear: the ''Aozora Maru'' was struck because the major powers converted a humanitarian evacuation corridor into a free-fire zone under Resolution 4940. We will not avenge three wounded sailors by offering up three thousand more to an imperialist quagmire. This cabinet will arm our ships with shields, not with invasion manifests. If the opposition wishes to vote for foreign ground interventions, they must first find an electorate willing to send their sons and daughters to die for the ruins of Rassentrennung."
</blockquote>

=== The OTWU strike ultimatum and ministerial cross-examination ===

The focus shifted rapidly to Transport Minister [[Seiran Mochizuki]] (OSP), a former railway union organiser, and Deputy Prime Minister [[Rento Nakayama]] (OSP), who were confronted with the OTWU's strike notice.

<blockquote>
'''Seiran Mochizuki (Transport Minister, OSP):''' "The government has received formal communication from the National Executive of the OTWU. Their position is entirely reasonable: commercial seafarers are not soldiers. They volunteered to rescue women and children fleeing ethnic cleansing under the emblem of the Adonian Community, not to serve as unprotected bait. We will not ask a single Sanese deckhand to hoist anchor until this Diet enacts statutory civilian protections and defensive rules of engagement that empower our escorts to destroy incoming ordnance."
</blockquote>

Foreign Minister [[Kenichi Mori]] then addressed the chamber regarding the 20 October deconfliction leak:

<blockquote>
'''Kenichi Mori (Foreign Minister, OSP):''' "Staatsrat Chairman Kruse-Essert claimed that Okaiken drew the target maps for coalition aviation. That is an outright falsehood. Our consular mission in Yaweka passed transit coordinates for one purpose: to ensure that civilian hulls carrying desperate families were not blown out of the water by either side. When covert coordination is warped into wartime propaganda, the only remedy is radical transparency. That is why, earlier today in the Adonian Assembly, Okaiken formally submitted [[Adonian Community Resolution 4942D]], co-sponsored by our neighbors [[Yanbaru]] and [[Dagit]]. We are taking the safety corridors out of backroom cables and codifying them into international law, backed by a 15-nautical-mile mandatory exclusion zone and the right of our escorts to shoot down any missile fired at our ships."
</blockquote>

=== The SDP ultimatum ===

The debate reached its political climax when [[Shimane Yoshida]], leader of the coalition partner [[Social Democratic Party (Okaiken)|SDP]], took the rostrum. Holding the 36 votes necessary to sustain the government, Yoshida made the SDP's continuing coalition participation contingent on an ironclad ban on ground combat:

<blockquote>
'''Shimane Yoshida (SDP):''' "The SDP did not enter this coalition to become an auxiliary cheer squad for coalition airstrikes or landing operations. Reports that landing craft are assembling in the Strait of Sindewand should chill every person in this country who remembers the Great Adonian War. We say to the Prime Minister and to the Foreign Minister: the 36 members of the SDP will vote for defensive escort protections and refugee relief funds. But if one Sanese marine sets foot on Kaftian soil, or if one chartered ferry is requisitioned to carry coalition troops into Mabanda, the coalition agreement is torn up, and this government will fall before midnight."
</blockquote>

== The October Legislative Package ==

Overnight on 23 October, Cabinet Secretariat staff and parliamentary drafting committees finalized the four-bill '''"October Maritime Security and Non-Belligerence Legislative Package"''' ({{Nihongo|10月海上安全・不戦立法パッケージ|Jūgatsu Kaijō Anzen Fusen Rippō Pakkēji}}). The package was brought to the floor for a sequential vote on the afternoon of 24 October.

=== Emergency Maritime Civilian Protection Act ===
The '''Emergency Maritime Civilian Protection Act''' (海上民生航行保護及び護衛交戦規則緊急措置法) establishes statutory defensive rules of engagement (ROE), authorizing SIF escort warships forward-staged in Alwani logistics harbors to employ kinetic interceptors, close-in weapon systems (CIWS), and electronic countermeasures to shoot down incoming artillery shells, cruise missiles, and unmanned aerial vehicles targeting civilian evacuation vessels within a 15-nautical-mile radius. Its proportional suppression authority allows Sanese warships to return fire strictly against the specific shore battery, radar installation, or combat craft actively firing upon a convoy, prohibiting pre-emptive interdiction strikes and general shore bombardment. Its separation-of-command provisions mandate that Sanese naval units remain under sovereign national command liaised to the AC Secretariat, legally barring subordination to the JWG-PNK coalition headquarters at [[Joint Base Ajowa]].

=== Kaftian Relief and Seafarers' Compensation Act ===
The '''Kaftian Relief and Seafarers' Compensation Act''' (対カフティア人道難民支援及び被災船員特別補償法) formally appropriates I$480 million in emergency foreign assistance to the Adonian Community Hosting Fund for frontline refugee transit centers in [[Alwana]], matching the grant authorized under [[Adonian Community Resolution 4935]]. It establishes a comprehensive seafarers' indemnity — full state disability pensions, psychological trauma care, and hazard bonus multipliers — for the three injured crew members of the ''Aozora Maru'' and all Sanese merchant seamen operating in the Pfein Sea theatre, and legally enshrines the right of commercial ship crews to refuse transit through active combat corridors that lack certified ACOM-NK radar verification.

=== Diet Binding Resolution on Overseas Ground Non-Belligerence ===
The '''Diet Binding Resolution on Overseas Ground Non-Belligerence''' (海外地上武力介入不参加及び民間船舶軍事徴用禁止決議) formally resolves that Okaiken will not participate in, fund, or facilitate any ground intervention, amphibious landing, or territorial peacekeeping force in [[Wolffrea]] or [[Bonande]], binding cabinet delegates to vote against any such measure in the Adonian Assembly. It strictly forbids the Ministry of Defense from requisitioning civilian commercial ferries or merchant hulls for the transport of foreign or domestic troops, armaments, or offensive munitions.

=== Parliamentary Ratification of Draft AC Resolution 4942D ===
The '''Parliamentary Ratification of Draft AC Resolution 4942D''' (アドラ共同体第4942D号決議案推進に関する院内承認決議) gives formal Diet ratification to Okaiken's diplomatic offensive in the [[Adonian Assembly]], instructing the Sanese delegation to demand an immediate [[Adonian Community Observer Mission in Northern Kaftia]] (ACOM-NK) forensic investigation into the ''Aozora Maru'' shelling, statutory compensation from Bonande, and the creation of public 15-nautical-mile deconfliction zones.

== Floor votes and outcome ==

On the afternoon of 24 October 2026, the four measures were put to a roll-call vote.

Before voting commenced, the opposition bloc (LDP, PPO, OIP, and NKP) tabled a joint motion of no confidence against Foreign Minister Kenichi Mori, alleging "criminal diplomatic negligence" in the handling of the deconfliction coordinates. With the governing coalition holding firm and Independent [[Hayashi Akihiro]] voting with the cabinet, the censure motion was defeated:

