== Political aftermath ==

The passage of the package averted both a catastrophic maritime general strike by the OTWU and the collapse of the Ikazaki Cabinet. The OTWU withdrew its strike notice on the evening of 24 October, and the ''ISN Shirakumo'' was formally assigned under the new defensive ROE, successfully escorting the subsequent civilian evacuation convoy from Alwani transit ports without further merchant casualties. Armed with a binding parliamentary mandate, Okaiken circulated draft [[Adonian Community Resolution 4942D]] in the Adonian Assembly with co-sponsors [[Yanbaru]] and [[Dagit]], establishing the international legal framework for the 15-nautical-mile safe shipping lanes and neutralizing accusations of unilateral bias. The crisis demonstrated the viability — and the fragility — of the SCP–OSP–SDP coalition: while Prime Minister Ikazaki demonstrated parliamentary resilience, the intense cross-examination solidified the "Yoshida–Ikazaki red line", cementing Okaiken's formal parliamentary consensus of robust humanitarian naval escort abroad but absolute non-intervention in foreign ground warfare.

On the evening of 24 October, confirmation reached Okami that the Sindewand delegation had submitted draft [[Adonian Community Resolution 4942E]] to the Adonian Assembly, proposing the condemnation of Okaiken for the escort deployment, economic sanctions on the state, and personal sanctions on the Prime Minister. The House of Commoners convened an extraordinary session the same night and adopted the [[October 2026 Diet emergency resolution on the Wolffrean War|October 2026 Diet emergency resolution]] rejecting the Sindewand draft's characterisation of the escort flotilla and directing the continued promotion of Resolution 4942D; the resolution passed 437–18, with only the Okaiken Innovation Party opposed.

